TensorFlow defines the XNNPACK repository this build uses (LiteRT's own
definition is skipped: TensorFlow's comes first). This adds our XNNPACK patch
to it (patch_c_api.sh section 21). The hunk names the pinned archive, so a
TensorFlow that moves XNNPACK fails the fetch until the XNNPACK patch is
re-checked. Strip 0, like third_party/tensorflow/tensorflow.patch.

--- third_party/xla/third_party/xnnpack/workspace.bzl	2026-11-02 08:45:31
+++ third_party/xla/third_party/xnnpack/workspace.bzl	2026-11-02 08:45:31
@@ -24,5 +24,6 @@
         sha256 = "b1d4ab092cd92b1241c1d14f440b5ed725530757b540fe4fb88a20b07577e8a8",
         strip_prefix = "XNNPACK-28d1fc6d908bc4d80920be989177b7eb1a4aebc8",
         urls = tf_mirror_urls("https://github.com/google/XNNPACK/archive/28d1fc6d908bc4d80920be989177b7eb1a4aebc8.zip"),
+        patch_file = ["@//:flutter_gemma_xnnpack_pf32_sme2_apple.patch"],
     )
     # LINT.ThenChange(//tensorflow/lite/tools/cmake/modules/xnnpack.cmake)
